From: Kartheek E <karte@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: 16 Sep 2026
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: add 11bi CPE security configurations for AP mode

WiFi8/11bi: Add 11bi Client Privacy Enhancement (CPE)
support in AP
New Security object parameters under WiFi.AccessPoint.{i}.Security:
  - EPPKE: Enable EPPKE AKM in RSNE of beacons/probe responses
  - AssocFrameEncryption: (Re)Association frame encryption support
  - PMKSACachingPrivacy: PMKID caching privacy to prevent device tracking
  - KEKInPASN: Unauthenticated EPPKE without base AKM
  - EAPUsingAuthenticationFrames: EAP using 802.11 authentication frames (enterprise)
  - SAEPwIdNum/SAEPwIdKey: SAE password identifier changing support
  - PASNGroups: PASN elliptic curve groups for EPPKE authentication
  - RadSecEnable/RadSecCACert/RadSecClientCert/RadSecPrivateKey: RADSec
    (RADIUS over TLS, RFC 6614) for enterprise deployments

Signed-off-by: Karteek E <karte@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
